    Question
   The Nautilus application development team was working on a git repository /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo present on Storage server in Stratos DC. However, they reported an issue with the recent commits being pushed to this repo. They have asked the DevOps team to revert repo HEAD to last commit. Below are more details about the task:

 1-In /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo git repository, revert the latest commit ( HEAD ) to the previous commit (JFYI the previous commit hash should be with initial commit message ).
 2-Use revert demo message (please use all small letters for commit message) for the new revert commit.

  Solution
 1- Login into the storage server
  - Enter the repo
      cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo
  -Check commit history
     sudo git log --oneline
 2- Revert HEAD to the latest commit
     sudo git revert HEAD -m 1 -n
  - Commit with required message
     sudo git commit -m "revert demo"
  - Check commit history
     sudo git log --oneline
  - Push the change back to th remote
     sudo git push origin HEAD
